{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
Sets the mode, monitor, video mode and placement of a window. }}\par
{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
This function sets the monitor that the window uses for full screen mode or, if the monitor is {\f2 NULL} , makes it windowed mode.\par
When setting a monitor, this function updates the width, height and refresh rate of the desired video mode and switches to the video mode closest to it. The window position is ignored when setting a monitor.\par
When the monitor is {\f2 NULL} , the position, width and height are used to place the window content area. The refresh rate is ignored when no monitor is specified.\par
If you only wish to update the resolution of a full screen window or the size of a windowed mode window, see {\b glfwSetWindowSize}.\par
When a window transitions from full screen to windowed mode, this function restores any previous window settings such as whether it is decorated, floating, resizable, has size or aspect ratio limits, etc.\par
